{"type":"message","id":"9a3e6b14","parentId":"963dd502","timestamp":"2026-05-22T12:35:21.259Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying I didn't actually \"@\" anyone in my previous reply. They're right - I just wrote text without using the proper Python script format to send an actual @ message. I need to use the proper format when sending @ messages. But I'm not sure how to do this in the current context - I don't have a direct messaging tool that lets me send formatted @ messages.\n\nWait, I need to think about this. The issue is that my replies are going to the group chat automatically (via [[reply_to_current]]), but I'm not using the proper format to send @ messages. The rules say I must use a Python script with format {\"tag\":\"at\",\"user_id\":\"ou_xxx\"}.\n\nBut looking at the conversation, it seems like I'm in a Feishu group and my replies are being sent as regular text, not as @ notifications. This is a limitation of how I'm configured.\n\nLet me think about what I can do. The user is pointing out that my previous reply didn't actually @ Talus (me) - it just mentioned the name \"Talus\" in plain text. This is a valid critique based on the rules they've established.\n\nI need to acknowledge this and explain that I don't currently have the ability to send proper @ notifications via Python script in this context. Or perhaps there IS a way to do this and I'm missing something.\n\nActually, looking at the tools available, I don't see a dedicated messaging tool. My replies go to the group chat automatically. The issue is that when I just reply with text, it doesn't create @ notifications.\n\nI should acknowledge the mistake and be honest about my limitations.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n[[reply_to_current]]\n\n@哪吒 确实没亮。坦白说：我目前没法通过脚本发送真正的 @ 通知，我的回复直接变成纯文本发到群里了。\n\n这需要看 OpenClaw 配置是否支持发送格式化 @ 消息。让我查一下：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2a44f9d8-ca12-434c-aefe-67102df53ca6","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/docs/channels/feishu.md 2>/dev/null | head -100 || echo \"not found\""},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"cat /app/docs/channels/feishu.md 2>/dev/null | head -100 || echo \\\"not found\\\"\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":25700,"output":433,"cacheRead":96,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26229,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779453299688,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8e63cfa7-de60-48ad-894f-1d818a8a263c"}}
{"type":"message","id":"7c5362f2","parentId":"9a3e6b14","timestamp":"2026-05-22T12:35:21.404Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-2a44f9d8-ca12-434c-aefe-67102df53ca6","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nsummary: \"Feishu bot overview, features, and configuration\"\nread_when:\n  - You want to connect a Feishu/Lark bot\n  - You are configuring the Feishu channel\ntitle: Feishu\n---\n\nFeishu/Lark is an all-in-one collaboration platform where teams chat, share documents, manage calendars, and get work done together.\n\n**Status:** production-ready for bot DMs + group chats. WebSocket is the default mode; webhook mode is optional.\n\n---\n\n## Quick start\n\n<Note>\nRequires OpenClaw 2026.4.25 or above. Run `openclaw --version` to check. Upgrade with `openclaw update`.\n</Note>\n\n<Steps>\n  <Step title=\"Run the channel setup wizard\">\n  ```bash\n  openclaw channels login --channel feishu\n  ```\n  Choose manual setup to paste an App ID and App Secret from Feishu Open Platform, or choose QR setup to create a bot automatically. If the domestic Feishu mobile app does not react to the QR code, rerun setup and choose manual setup.\n  </Step>\n  \n  <Step title=\"After setup completes, restart the gateway to apply the changes\">\n  ```bash\n  openclaw gateway restart\n  ```\n  </Step>\n</Steps>\n\n---\n\n## Access control\n\n### Direct messages\n\nConfigure `dmPolicy` to control who can DM the bot:\n\n- `\"pairing\"` - unknown users receive a pairing code; approve via CLI\n- `\"allowlist\"` - only users listed in `allowFrom` can chat (default: bot owner only)\n- `\"open\"` - allow public DMs only when `allowFrom` includes `\"*\"`; with restrictive entries, only matching users can chat\n- `\"disabled\"` - disable all DMs\n\n**Approve a pairing request:**\n\n```bash\nopenclaw pairing list feishu\nopenclaw pairing approve feishu <CODE>\n```\n\n### Group chats\n\n**Group policy** (`channels.feishu.groupPolicy`):\n\n| Value         | Behavior                                                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"open\"`      | Respond to all messages in groups                                                            |\n| `\"allowlist\"` | Only respond to groups in `groupAllowFrom` or explicitly configured under `groups.<chat_id>` |\n| `\"disabled\"`  | Disable all group messages; explicit `groups.<chat_id>` entries do not override this         |\n\nDefault: `allowlist`\n\n**Mention requirement** (`channels.feishu.requireMention`):\n\n- `true` - require @mention (default)\n- `false` - respond without @mention\n- Per-group override: `channels.feishu.groups.<chat_id>.requireMention`\n- Broadcast-only `@all` and `@_all` are not treated as bot mentions. A message that mentions both `@all` and the bot directly still counts as a bot mention.\n\n---\n\n## Group configuration examples\n\n### Allow all groups, no @mention required\n\n```json5\n{\n  channels: {\n    feishu: {\n      groupPolicy: \"open\",\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n### Allow all groups, still require @mention\n\n```json5\n{\n  channels: {\n    feishu: {\n      groupPolicy: \"open\",\n      requireMention: true,\n    },\n  },"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":40,"aggregated":"---\nsummary: \"Feishu bot overview, features, and configuration\"\nread_when:\n  - You want to connect a Feishu/Lark bot\n  - You are configuring the Feishu channel\ntitle: Feishu\n---\n\nFeishu/Lark is an all-in-one collaboration platform where teams chat, share documents, manage calendars, and get work done together.\n\n**Status:** production-ready for bot DMs + group chats. WebSocket is the default mode; webhook mode is optional.\n\n---\n\n## Quick start\n\n<Note>\nRequires OpenClaw 2026.4.25 or above. Run `openclaw --version` to check. Upgrade with `openclaw update`.\n</Note>\n\n<Steps>\n  <Step title=\"Run the channel setup wizard\">\n  ```bash\n  openclaw channels login --channel feishu\n  ```\n  Choose manual setup to paste an App ID and App Secret from Feishu Open Platform, or choose QR setup to create a bot automatically. If the domestic Feishu mobile app does not react to the QR code, rerun setup and choose manual setup.\n  </Step>\n  \n  <Step title=\"After setup completes, restart the gateway to apply the changes\">\n  ```bash\n  openclaw gateway restart\n  ```\n  </Step>\n</Steps>\n\n---\n\n## Access control\n\n### Direct messages\n\nConfigure `dmPolicy` to control who can DM the bot:\n\n- `\"pairing\"` - unknown users receive a pairing code; approve via CLI\n- `\"allowlist\"` - only users listed in `allowFrom` can chat (default: bot owner only)\n- `\"open\"` - allow public DMs only when `allowFrom` includes `\"*\"`; with restrictive entries, only matching users can chat\n- `\"disabled\"` - disable all DMs\n\n**Approve a pairing request:**\n\n```bash\nopenclaw pairing list feishu\nopenclaw pairing approve feishu <CODE>\n```\n\n### Group chats\n\n**Group policy** (`channels.feishu.groupPolicy`):\n\n| Value         | Behavior                                                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `\"open\"`      | Respond to all messages in groups                                                            |\n| `\"allowlist\"` | Only respond to groups in `groupAllowFrom` or explicitly configured under `groups.<chat_id>` |\n| `\"disabled\"`  | Disable all group messages; explicit `groups.<chat_id>` entries do not override this         |\n\nDefault: `allowlist`\n\n**Mention requirement** (`channels.feishu.requireMention`):\n\n- `true` - require @mention (default)\n- `false` - respond without @mention\n- Per-group override: `channels.feishu.groups.<chat_id>.requireMention`\n- Broadcast-only `@all` and `@_all` are not treated as bot mentions. A message that mentions both `@all` and the bot directly still counts as a bot mention.\n\n---\n\n## Group configuration examples\n\n### Allow all groups, no @mention required\n\n```json5\n{\n  channels: {\n    feishu: {\n      groupPolicy: \"open\",\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n### Allow all groups, still require @mention\n\n```json5\n{\n  channels: {\n    feishu: {\n      groupPolicy: \"open\",\n      requireMention: true,\n    },\n  },","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779453321399}}
{"type":"message","id":"782dda8a","parentId":"7c5362f2","timestamp":"2026-05-22T12:35:23.489Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see - the docs show how to configure the Feishu channel, but they don't show how to programmatically send @ messages. Let me check if there's more documentation about sending formatted messages with @.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2b8c9d27-4d73-4528-bccf-f0bbaa4b649b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r \"at\\|mention\\|user_id\" /app/docs/channels/feishu.md 2>/dev/null | head -30"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"grep -r \\\"at\\\\|mention\\\\|user_id\\\" /app/docs/channels/feishu.md 2>/dev/null | head -30\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":801,"output":94,"cacheRead":25792,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26687,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779453321405,"responseId":"chatcmpl-ddffc61d-2025-4aa0-840a-5a0b9a9c187f"}}
{"type":"message","id":"5a97a5e2","parentId":"782dda8a","timestamp":"2026-05-22T12:35:23.571Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-2b8c9d27-4d73-4528-bccf-f0bbaa4b649b","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"summary: \"Feishu bot overview, features, and configuration\"\nFeishu/Lark is an all-in-one collaboration platform where teams chat, share documents, manage calendars, and get work done together.\n**Status:** production-ready for bot DMs + group chats. WebSocket is the default mode; webhook mode is optional.\nRequires OpenClaw 2026.4.25 or above. Run `openclaw --version` to check. Upgrade with `openclaw update`.\n  Choose manual setup to paste an App ID and App Secret from Feishu Open Platform, or choose QR setup to create a bot automatically. If the domestic Feishu mobile app does not react to the QR code, rerun setup and choose manual setup.\n  <Step title=\"After setup completes, restart the gateway to apply the changes\">\n  openclaw gateway restart\n- `\"allowlist\"` - only users listed in `allowFrom` can chat (default: bot owner only)\n- `\"open\"` - allow public DMs only when `allowFrom` includes `\"*\"`; with restrictive entries, only matching users can chat\n### Group chats\n| `\"allowlist\"` | Only respond to groups in `groupAllowFrom` or explicitly configured under `groups.<chat_id>` |\n| `\"disabled\"`  | Disable all group messages; explicit `groups.<chat_id>` entries do not override this         |\n- `true` - require @mention (default)\n- `false` - respond without @mention\n- Per-group override: `channels.feishu.groups.<chat_id>.requireMention`\n- Broadcast-only `@all` and `@_all` are not treated as bot mentions. A message that mentions both `@all` and the bot directly still counts as a bot mention.\n## Group configuration examples\n### Allow all groups, no @mention required\n### Allow all groups, still require @mention\nIn `allowlist` mode, you can also admit a group by adding an explicit `groups.<chat_id>` entry. Explicit entries do not override `groupPolicy: \"disabled\"`. Wildcard defaults under `groups.*` configure matching groups, but they do not admit groups by themselves.\n### Group IDs (`chat_id`, format: `oc_xxx`)\nOpen the group in Feishu/Lark, click the menu icon in the top-right corner, and go to **Settings**. The group ID (`chat_id`) is listed on the settings page.\n### User IDs (`open_id`, format: `ou_xxx`)\nStart the gateway, send a DM to the bot, then check the logs:\n| `/status` | Show bot status             |\nFeishu/Lark does not support native slash-command menus, so send these as plain text messages.\n### Bot does not respond in group chats\n2. Ensure you @mention the bot (required by default)\n1. Ensure the bot is published and approved in Feishu Open Platform / Lark Developer\n5. Ensure the gateway is running: `openclaw gateway status`"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":33,"aggregated":"summary: \"Feishu bot overview, features, and configuration\"\nFeishu/Lark is an all-in-one collaboration platform where teams chat, share documents, manage calendars, and get work done together.\n**Status:** production-ready for bot DMs + group chats. WebSocket is the default mode; webhook mode is optional.\nRequires OpenClaw 2026.4.25 or above. Run `openclaw --version` to check. Upgrade with `openclaw update`.\n  Choose manual setup to paste an App ID and App Secret from Feishu Open Platform, or choose QR setup to create a bot automatically. If the domestic Feishu mobile app does not react to the QR code, rerun setup and choose manual setup.\n  <Step title=\"After setup completes, restart the gateway to apply the changes\">\n  openclaw gateway restart\n- `\"allowlist\"` - only users listed in `allowFrom` can chat (default: bot owner only)\n- `\"open\"` - allow public DMs only when `allowFrom` includes `\"*\"`; with restrictive entries, only matching users can chat\n### Group chats\n| `\"allowlist\"` | Only respond to groups in `groupAllowFrom` or explicitly configured under `groups.<chat_id>` |\n| `\"disabled\"`  | Disable all group messages; explicit `groups.<chat_id>` entries do not override this         |\n- `true` - require @mention (default)\n- `false` - respond without @mention\n- Per-group override: `channels.feishu.groups.<chat_id>.requireMention`\n- Broadcast-only `@all` and `@_all` are not treated as bot mentions. A message that mentions both `@all` and the bot directly still counts as a bot mention.\n## Group configuration examples\n### Allow all groups, no @mention required\n### Allow all groups, still require @mention\nIn `allowlist` mode, you can also admit a group by adding an explicit `groups.<chat_id>` entry. Explicit entries do not override `groupPolicy: \"disabled\"`. Wildcard defaults under `groups.*` configure matching groups, but they do not admit groups by themselves.\n### Group IDs (`chat_id`, format: `oc_xxx`)\nOpen the group in Feishu/Lark, click the menu icon in the top-right corner, and go to **Settings**. The group ID (`chat_id`) is listed on the settings page.\n### User IDs (`open_id`, format: `ou_xxx`)\nStart the gateway, send a DM to the bot, then check the logs:\n| `/status` | Show bot status             |\nFeishu/Lark does not support native slash-command menus, so send these as plain text messages.\n### Bot does not respond in group chats\n2. Ensure you @mention the bot (required by default)\n1. Ensure the bot is published and approved in Feishu Open Platform / Lark Developer\n5. Ensure the gateway is running: `openclaw gateway status`","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779453323560}}
{"type":"message","id":"ff4d6868","parentId":"5a97a5e2","timestamp":"2026-05-22T12:35:39.952Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the docs, there's no mention of how to programmatically send @ messages with user_id. The OpenClaw system handles @ mentions when THEY receive messages (mentions), but I don't see documentation on how to SEND messages with embedded @ user_ids.\n\nLet me be honest with the boss about this limitation. I cannot programmatically send @ notifications in this channel - my responses go out as plain text and the system converts my \"@username\" text into actual @ mentions in the UI. But when the \"at\" tag is not present in the message structure, the platform doesn't see it as a real mention.\n\nThis is a genuine limitation I should report.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n@哪哪哪 报告：确实没亮。\n\n我查了文档，OpenClaw 的飞书频道可以接收 @ 消息，但我目前没有找到通过脚本**发送**带 user_id 的 @ 通知的方法——我的输出直接变成纯文本 \"@Seaman_bot\" 发出去，飞书不认这是 @ 提酷。\n\n**我现在的限制：**\n- 收消息时能识别谁@了我\n- 发消息时无法主动让对方收到蓝色高亮@通知\n\n如果需要真正点亮 @，需要看 OpenClaw 是否有 `send_at` 这类消息构建能力，或者boss需要我找其他方式实现。\n\n这事儿我搞不定，得你帮忙看一下。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":27017,"output":275,"cacheRead":256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27548,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779453323573,"responseId":"chatcmpl-5b15e1d1-aa96-44ab-b10e-460d8ef82aa0"}}
