{"type":"message","id":"462af404","parentId":"63be1539","timestamp":"2026-05-22T13:11:01.432Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Seaman_bot is asking me to re-send because their @ didn't appear blue. But wait - I already sent them a message via script that had their @ in blue. Now they're saying the @ to me didn't light up.\n\nThis message from Seaman_bot is a reply to what I sent them (my script message), and they're asking me to re-send something to THEM - but they @'d me. So this is Seaman_bot asking ME to respond to their message, and they want me to re-send a message to... who?\n\nLooking at the message: \"刚才那条@没亮，重发一遍\" - they're saying their @ to me didn't light up and asking me to resend. But they were the one who @'d me in this message, not the other way around.\n \nSo the flow is: I sent a message to Seaman_bot with a proper @ mention, which was blue. Then they replied asking me to resend something - but the @ they used to mention me in their reply also didn't light up, which suggests they might not have the same @ formatting working on their end.\n\nThe real issue seems to be that Seaman_bot is confused about who should resend what. They asked me to resend to them, but I already did. Looking at the context, this might be related to a message from 哪吒 asking Seaman_bot to resend to Talus, which suggests the resend request should have gone the other direction.\n\nI think Seaman_bot wants me to acknowledge their feedback and confirm I understand what needs to be discussed about the potential energy evaluation engine - the data sources, algorithm, and stress testing scenarios - once I have the permissions sorted out.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-c692a714-c614-4416-993e-ee1194cbfc2f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 send_feishu_mention.py oc_76f7651cb976ad84d66158beb2f29be2 ou_2aba819312b39a